1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:06,300
Here we are in a clear bull trend above the moving average.

2
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:12,000
Look at this bar, a strong bull trend bar closing near its high.

3
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,400
These three bars form a tight pullback.

4
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:18,800
This is the second entry buy setup.

5
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,600
I would buy here above the signal bar.

6
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:26,000
Now this one is harder to read.

7
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:29,400
These bars show the market going sideways.

8
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:32,700
This breakout failed quickly.

9
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:36,100
And this bar trapped the late bulls.

10
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:39,500
Notice how the moving average flattened out.

11
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:45,700
This is a trading range, so we expect reversals.

12
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:49,100
This bar is the first push down.

13
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:52,400
This wedge has three pushes.

14
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:57,300
I would not take this trade because the location is poor.

15
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,600
Look at this bar here.

16
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:04,400
These two bars are an outside up pattern.

17
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:07,700
This pullback is shallow.

18
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:11,500
Was it this bar or the next one?

19
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:14,900
This failed breakout is the sell signal.

20
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:18,300
That is the end of the lesson.

